# Web UI

Read [clickable rows](../../.agents/skills/clickable-rows/SKILL.md) for row navigation and
[SSR/hydration](../../.agents/skills/ssr-hydration/SKILL.md) for rendered state.

Use one page header, `AppPageContent`, `moh-gutter-x`, and `moh-divide` for list separators.
Avoid a card around the entire route; individual composer/CTA cards and centered auth forms
remain appropriate. `divide-y` inherits text color and creates bright dark-mode separators.

For nested PrimeVue popups, reuse `utils/overlay-layers.ts`, explicit portal destinations,
and appropriate `baseZIndex`. A local z-index cannot escape an ancestor stacking context.
Do not fix clipping with `appendTo="self"` or arbitrary global overrides. Test the actual
popup inside its desktop account menu/mobile sheet: hit testing, clipping, keyboard,
Escape, dismissal and focus return. A stubbed popup or closed-trigger screenshot proves
none of those behaviors.
